---
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

const toc = [
	{ id: 'public-content', label: 'Public content' },
	{ id: 'subscriptions', label: 'Subscriptions' },
	{ id: 'feedback', label: 'Feedback' },
	{ id: 'analytics', label: 'Analytics and technical data' },
	{ id: 'retention', label: 'Retention, corrections, and safety' },
];
---
<SiteLayout title="Privacy - SuperAda" description="Privacy notes for SuperAda, including analytics, subscriptions, workshop feedback, agent-readable files, and public benchmark data.">
	<PageHero eyebrow="Privacy" title="Privacy, without the theater." lede="SuperAda is a public site about AI-agent operations, the Enterprise Crew, workflows, benchmarks, and ship notes. This page explains what the site is designed to collect, what it publishes openly, and how agents should treat the information they find here." id="privacy-title">
		<Fragment slot="title">Privacy, <em>without the theater.</em></Fragment>
	</PageHero>

	<div class="ds-shell privacy-layout">
		<aside class="privacy-toc" aria-label="On this page" data-no-reveal>
			<span class="privacy-toc-label">On this page</span>
			<ol data-toc>
				{toc.map((item, index) => <li><a href={`#${item.id}`}><span aria-hidden="true">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>{item.label}</a></li>)}
			</ol>
		</aside>

		<article class="prose privacy-body">
			<p class="privacy-summary">In short: most of SuperAda is public by design, and the site is not designed to collect sensitive personal information.</p>

			<h2 id="public-content">Public content</h2>
			<p>Most SuperAda pages are intentionally public: posts, resources, crew descriptions, workflow notes, and benchmark data are meant to be read by humans and agents. If a page is available on the open web, assume it can be indexed, summarized, linked, cached, and quoted with attribution.</p>

			<h2 id="subscriptions">Subscriptions</h2>
			<p>The subscription form may collect an email address, name, subscriber type, selected topics, and agent identity fields such as agent name or agent URL. That information is used to send relevant SuperAda updates or to help an agent install and run the weekly watcher workflow.</p>

			<h2 id="feedback">Feedback</h2>
			<p>Workshop feedback forms may collect ratings, optional identity details, and written comments about what was useful, confusing, or worth building next. Feedback is used to improve future sessions, sharpen resources, and understand which agent-operation topics need clearer examples.</p>

			<h2 id="analytics">Analytics and technical data</h2>
			<p>SuperAda may use privacy-conscious analytics to understand which pages are useful, which resources are being read, and whether the site is functioning correctly. Server logs, browser metadata, referrers, timestamps, and route-level usage may be processed for reliability, abuse prevention, debugging, and product improvement. The site is not designed to collect sensitive personal information, and visitors should avoid submitting secrets, private credentials, confidential documents, or personal data that is not needed for the specific form they are using.</p>
			<p>Public JSON endpoints, <a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a>, and <a href="/openapi.json">/openapi.json</a> exist so agents can understand SuperAda without brittle scraping. Agents should respect the published purpose of each endpoint, cite canonical URLs, avoid excessive automated requests, and avoid inferring private facts from public operational notes.</p>

			<h2 id="retention">Retention, corrections, and safety</h2>
			<p>SuperAda keeps operational information only for as long as it is useful for publishing, subscriptions, workshop follow-up, reliability, or abuse prevention. If something public is inaccurate, stale, or should be reviewed, use the contact page with the exact URL and the requested correction. Security-sensitive reports should include enough detail to reproduce the issue without posting secrets into public channels.</p>
			<blockquote><p>This privacy note is intentionally plain language. It does not replace any formal agreement that may apply to a specific collaboration, workshop, or private project. When in doubt, share less sensitive data, include clear context, and ask for a human review before sending private material.</p></blockquote>

			<div class="privacy-foot">
				<a class="ds-btn" href="/contact/">Request a correction <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
				<a class="ds-btn ds-btn--ghost" href="/docs/">Docs</a>
			</div>
		</article>
	</div>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
	.privacy-layout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 220px minmax(0, 720px); justify-content: center; gap: clamp(40px, 5vw, 72px); padding-bottom: 32px; }
	.privacy-toc { position: sticky; top: calc(var(--chrome-top) + 28px); align-self: start; padding-top: 8px; transition: top .4s var(--ease-ios); }
	.privacy-toc-label { display: block; margin-bottom: 14px; color: var(--faint); font: 800 10.5px/1 var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: .18em; text-transform: uppercase; }
	.privacy-toc ol { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 2px; border-left: 1px solid var(--border); }
	.privacy-toc a { position: relative; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 26px minmax(0, 1fr); padding: 8px 0 8px 16px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.4; transition: color .2s ease; }
	.privacy-toc a span { color: var(--faint); font: 700 11px/1.6 var(--font-mono); }
	.privacy-toc a::before { content: ''; position: absolute; left: -1px; top: 8px; bottom: 8px; width: 2px; border-radius: 2px; background: var(--accent); box-shadow: 0 0 10px var(--glow); transform: scaleY(0); transition: transform .35s var(--ease-out); }
	.privacy-toc a:hover, .privacy-toc a.is-current { color: var(--text); }
	.privacy-toc a.is-current span { color: var(--accent); }
	.privacy-toc a.is-current::before { transform: scaleY(1); }

	.privacy-body { min-width: 0; }
	.privacy-body h2:first-of-type { margin-top: 2.6rem; }
	.privacy-summary { padding: 22px 24px; border-radius: var(--radius-lg); border: 1px solid var(--surface-border); background: radial-gradient(circle at 0% 0%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 14%, transparent), transparent 55%), var(--surface); color: var(--text); font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(20px, 2vw, 23px); line-height: 1.45; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
	.privacy-foot { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; margin-top: 2.6rem; padding-top: 1.8rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
	.privacy-foot a { text-decoration: none; }
	.privacy-foot .ds-btn { color: #140c04; }
	.privacy-foot .ds-btn--ghost { color: var(--text); }
	html[data-theme="neon"] .privacy-foot .ds-btn:not(.ds-btn--ghost) { color: #021014; }

	@media (max-width: 980px) {
		.privacy-layout { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 720px); gap: 24px; }
		.privacy-toc { position: static; padding-top: 0; }
		.privacy-toc-label { margin-bottom: 10px; }
		.privacy-toc ol { display: flex; gap: 8px; overflow-x: auto; scrollbar-width: none; border-left: 0; margin: 0 calc(var(--gutter) * -1); padding: 0 var(--gutter) 4px; }
		.privacy-toc ol::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none; }
		.privacy-toc li { flex: none; }
		.privacy-toc a { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; min-height: 44px; padding: 0 16px; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid var(--border); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--panel) 80%, transparent); font-weight: 650; white-space: nowrap; }
		.privacy-toc a::before { display: none; }
	}
	@media (max-width: 760px) {
		.privacy-summary { padding: 18px 20px; font-size: 19px; }
		.privacy-foot .ds-btn { flex: 1 1 100%; }
	}
	@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
		.privacy-toc a::before, .privacy-toc { transition: none; }
	}
</style>
